{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 598 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "8cb6600ff3d599aaa5ede02b9096f7f851a64cc8b77325b1dafbd5e87490772a" :edb/db-before-t 597 :edb/db-after-t 598 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533910 50 #inst "2026-10-05T11:19:47.016Z" 13194139533910 true] [17592186054590 1020 #edb/ref 17592186265227 13194139533910 true] [17592186054590 1020 #edb/ref 17592186265250 13194139533910 true] [17592186054759 1020 #edb/ref 17592186265234 13194139533910 true] [17592186054759 1020 #edb/ref 17592186265243 13194139533910 true] [17592186054760 1020 #edb/ref 17592186265238 13194139533910 true] [17592186265227 1017 #edb/ref 17592186265228 13194139533910 true] [17592186265227 1089 "q-108509" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265227 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533910 true] [17592186265227 1100 "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for ${x}^{3}{e}^{y}=9{x}^{4}.$" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265227 1113 #uuid "a9609c42-40f2-5fc7-9701-78545366cca4" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265227 1145 "First, we differentiate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ assuming that $y=y(x).$\n\nNote that to differentiate the ${x}^{3}{e}^{y}$ term, we will need to use the product rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}{e}^{y} & =9{x}^{4} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3}{e}^{y}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(9{x}^{4}) \\\\ [({x}^{3})({e}^{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})+(3{x}^{2})({e}^{y})] & =36{x}^{3} \\\\ {x}^{3}\\,{e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3{x}^{2}{e}^{y} & =36{x}^{3}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we solve the equation for $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}{e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3{x}^{2}{e}^{y} & =36{x}^{3} \\\\ {x}^{3}{e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =36{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}{e}^{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{36{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}{e}^{y}}{{x}^{3}{e}^{y}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{36}{{e}^{y}}-\\frac{3}{x}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265228 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265229 13194139533910 true] [17592186265228 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265230 13194139533910 true] [17592186265228 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265231 13194139533910 true] [17592186265228 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265232 13194139533910 true] [17592186265228 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265233 13194139533910 true] [17592186265228 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533910 true] [17592186265228 1041 "selection" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265228 1104 #edb/ref 17592186265229 13194139533910 true] [17592186265228 1110 #uuid "ceb0cdd7-0e15-58c7-ac08-b352259d01c9" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265229 1034 "\\frac{36}{{e}^{y}}-\\frac{3}{x}" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265229 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533910 true] [17592186265229 1111 #uuid "c578c4d7-051e-517c-8298-7ea4f24aa53a" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265230 1034 "\\frac{1}{{e}^{3y}}-\\frac{36}{x}" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265230 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533910 true] [17592186265230 1111 #uuid "4c80349a-e796-5b49-9136-5d4dcbd73d18" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265231 1034 "\\frac{36}{{e}^{y}}+\\frac{3}{{x}^{3}}" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265231 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533910 true] [17592186265231 1111 #uuid "a5875d47-4d1e-580f-af0a-ec9de6686a1f" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265232 1034 "-\\frac{6}{{e}^{y}}-\\frac{3}{x}" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265232 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533910 true] [17592186265232 1111 #uuid "e91fcc8c-08f8-5706-ad03-65f422aa5b71" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265233 1034 "\\frac{12}{{e}^{y}}+\\frac{{e}^{y}}{x}" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265233 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533910 true] [17592186265233 1111 #uuid "8bf7aa12-8290-5914-98bc-c52907e30ac5" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265234 1017 #edb/ref 17592186265235 13194139533910 true] [17592186265234 1089 "q-342311" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265234 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533910 true] [17592186265234 1100 "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent at the point $(1,1)$ for the curve $2{y}^{3}+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}-{x}^{3}=2.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265234 1113 #uuid "664421d1-b6cf-5b38-b99d-fead10a1505f" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265234 1145 "To find the slope at a point, we use implicit differentiation to calculate the derivative of the curve, assuming that $y=y(x).$\n\nNote that to differentiate the ${x}^{2}{y}^{2}$ term, we will need to use the product rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{y}^{3}+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}-{x}^{3} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{y}^{3}+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}-{x}^{3}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{y}^{3})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}{y}^{2})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2) \\\\ 6{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+[2x{y}^{2}+2{x}^{2}y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}]-3{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 6{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2x{y}^{2}+2{x}^{2}y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ (6{y}^{2}+2{x}^{2}y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}-2x{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}-2x{y}^{2}}{6{y}^{2}+2{x}^{2}y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent at the point $(1,1)$ is then given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(1,1)} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{3{x}^{2}-2x{y}^{2}}{6{y}^{2}+2{x}^{2}y})|}_{(1,1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(1)^{2}-2(1)(1)^{2}}{6(1)^{2}+2(1)^{2}(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265235 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265236 13194139533910 true] [17592186265235 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265237 13194139533910 true] [17592186265235 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533910 true] [17592186265235 1041 "field-1" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265235 1104 #edb/ref 17592186265236 13194139533910 true] [17592186265235 1110 #uuid "8a781991-c5de-5fa5-9637-d5a3704ef0ba" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265236 1034 "\\frac{1}{8}" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265236 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533910 true] [17592186265236 1111 #uuid "13b4e657-8c26-5066-bf51-21b6c156d4e0" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265237 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265237 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533910 true] [17592186265237 1111 #uuid "6fe00fd4-8add-59cd-94c2-7fa56660c778" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265238 1017 #edb/ref 17592186265239 13194139533910 true] [17592186265238 1017 #edb/ref 17592186265241 13194139533910 true] [17592186265238 1089 "q-342526" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265238 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533910 true] [17592186265238 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951578/assets/d997ec4e099fc8be5b34a51bdfd0e9511915c348671d9832ed640f0ec4360602.png)\n\nThe equation $4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=15y$ represents an ellipse. The normal line at the point $(3,3)$ on the ellipse intersects the $x$-axis at the point $P.$ What are the coordinates of $P?$\n\nThe coordinates of $P$ are $($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$).$" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265238 1113 #uuid "b1e065ed-0e60-5ad9-910a-1be3816757d8" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265238 1145 "First of all, we need to find the slope of the normal line at the point $(3,3).$ Remember that the slope of the normal line, ${m}^{′},$ is the negative reciprocal of the slope of the tangent line:\n\n$$\n{m}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{m}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we will calculate the derivative using implicit differentiation, assuming that $y=y(x).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =15y \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(15y) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(15y) \\\\ 8x+2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =15\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-15\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-8x \\\\ (2y-15)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-8x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{8x}{2y-15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the slope of the tangent at the point $(3,3)$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(3,\\,3)} \\\\  & ={(-\\frac{8x}{2y-15})|}_{(3,\\,3)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8\\cdot 3}{2\\cdot 3-15} \\\\  & =-\\frac{24}{(-9)} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the normal line is\n\n$$\n{m}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{(\\frac{8}{3})}=-\\frac{3}{8}.\n$$\n\nWe can write the equation of the normal line at the point $(3,3)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & ={m}^{′}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-3 & =-\\frac{3}{8}(x-3) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{3}{8}x+\\frac{9}{8}+3 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{3}{8}x+\\frac{33}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we just need to find where this normal line intersects the $x$-axis. At the point $P$ the $y$-coordinate is $0,$ so we set $y=0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{3}{8}x+\\frac{33}{8} \\\\ 0 & =-\\frac{3}{8}x+\\frac{33}{8} \\\\ \\frac{3}{8}x & =\\frac{33}{8} \\\\ x & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of $P$ are $(11,\\,0).$" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265239 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265240 13194139533910 true] [17592186265239 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533910 true] [17592186265239 1041 "field-1" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265239 1104 #edb/ref 17592186265240 13194139533910 true] [17592186265239 1110 #uuid "e91b6226-f88d-5fe8-8113-12f5d3ffe42f" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265240 1034 "11" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265240 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533910 true] [17592186265240 1111 #uuid "43b44b4b-1ab8-5550-9503-193b9c0873f7" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265241 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265242 13194139533910 true] [17592186265241 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533910 true] [17592186265241 1041 "field-2" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265241 1104 #edb/ref 17592186265242 13194139533910 true] [17592186265241 1110 #uuid "6572fad2-9932-5d7a-bd82-4c77995f729d" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265242 1034 "0" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265242 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533910 true] [17592186265242 1111 #uuid "78ef8f5f-dd88-58ac-a699-f1755c634657" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265243 1017 #edb/ref 17592186265244 13194139533910 true] [17592186265243 1089 "q-53747" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265243 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533910 true] [17592186265243 1100 "Find the slope of the tangent at the point $(2,\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ for the curve $x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y)=\\sqrt{2}.$" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265243 1113 #uuid "51fb5d36-6953-51d7-a02c-c7ac944811b3" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265243 1145 "To find the slope at a point, we use implicit differentiation to calculate the derivative of the curve, assuming that $y=y(x).$\n\nNote that to differentiate the $x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y)$ term, we will need to use the product rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y)) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{2}) \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y))+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y)\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) & =0 \\\\ x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y) & =0 \\\\ x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y)}{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y)} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡(y)}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent at the point $(2,\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ is then given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}_{(2,\\pi /4)} \\\\  & ={(-\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡(y)}{x})}_{(2,\\pi /4)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265244 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265245 13194139533910 true] [17592186265244 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265246 13194139533910 true] [17592186265244 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265247 13194139533910 true] [17592186265244 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265248 13194139533910 true] [17592186265244 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265249 13194139533910 true] [17592186265244 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533910 true] [17592186265244 1041 "selection" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265244 1104 #edb/ref 17592186265245 13194139533910 true] [17592186265244 1110 #uuid "b51ffca5-2317-5ca5-8977-43f8243fb671" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265245 1034 "-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265245 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533910 true] [17592186265245 1111 #uuid "8ee77a49-29a9-5f05-bfa7-306d178446e8" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265246 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265246 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533910 true] [17592186265246 1111 #uuid "146a0a90-ccd5-5d05-9d07-a8d9ca20eca3" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265247 1034 "-\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265247 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533910 true] [17592186265247 1111 #uuid "ca5922b5-c066-57dd-bca4-aa594fc29456" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265248 1034 "1" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265248 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533910 true] [17592186265248 1111 #uuid "99dcaf29-b602-5e67-bbce-361ef8eb81f4" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265249 1034 "-1" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265249 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533910 true] [17592186265249 1111 #uuid "81bef90d-82dd-5b5a-9fa4-1cc1aa643420" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265250 1017 #edb/ref 17592186265251 13194139533910 true] [17592186265250 1089 "q-72213" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265250 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533910 true] [17592186265250 1100 "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y)+{y}^{3}=2{x}^{3}.$" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265250 1113 #uuid "f84fff36-2406-5dc5-8004-29d635957982" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265250 1145 "First, we differentiate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ assuming that $y=y(x).$\n\nNote that to differentiate the $x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y$ term, we will need to use the product rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y)+{y}^{3}=2{x}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y)+{y}^{3}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y))+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{3}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{3}) \\\\ [x(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y)]+3{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6{x}^{2} \\\\ x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y)+3{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we solve the equation for $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6{x}^{2}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}(x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y)+3{y}^{2}) & =6{x}^{2}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{6{x}^{2}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y)}{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y)+3{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265251 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265252 13194139533910 true] [17592186265251 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265253 13194139533910 true] [17592186265251 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265254 13194139533910 true] [17592186265251 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265255 13194139533910 true] [17592186265251 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265256 13194139533910 true] [17592186265251 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533910 true] [17592186265251 1041 "selection" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265251 1104 #edb/ref 17592186265255 13194139533910 true] [17592186265251 1110 #uuid "df9fe65b-4b2c-5776-805c-35dea9340d86" 13194139533910 true] [17592186265252 1034 "\\frac{6{x}^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y)}{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y)+{y}^{2}}" 13194139533910